From: Mikhail Mlhcnn <mikhail@advnirr.org>
Subject: [PATCH] SurfaceFlinger: do not mode-set a powered-off display

Rebased for Android 17 (Evolution X cnb) bundled multi-display modeset loop:
mark shouldDropModeRequests/canApplyAllModes when !display->isPoweredOn() so
pending mode requests are dropped through the standard cleanup path instead of
driving MediaTek composer into a 144 Hz screen-off vsync storm.

diff --git a/services/surfaceflinger/SurfaceFlinger.cpp b/services/surfaceflinger/SurfaceFlinger.cpp
index e1b4943..44edb15 100644
--- a/services/surfaceflinger/SurfaceFlinger.cpp
+++ b/services/surfaceflinger/SurfaceFlinger.cpp
@@ -1720,6 +1720,18 @@ void SurfaceFlinger::initiateDisplayModeChanges() {
             }
             auto& desiredMode = desiredModeIt->second;
 
+            // Do not drive a mode set into a powered-off panel. It cannot be completed
+            // there, and on MediaTek the composer answers such a request by emitting
+            // vsync callbacks for the requested timeline forever - measured at ~143/s
+            // with the screen off, pinning SurfaceFlinger at ~18% of a core until the
+            // display powers back on. Drop the request instead; policy re-evaluates on
+            // power-on.
+            if (!display->isPoweredOn()) {
+                shouldDropModeRequests = true;
+                canApplyAllModes = false;
+                continue;
+            }
+
             const auto desiredModeId = desiredMode.mode.modePtr->getId();
             const auto displayModePtrOpt =
                     mPhysicalDisplays.get(displayId)
